# Neovim runtime artifacts. nvim writes these into its own config dir, which is
# the folded symlink target — so they land here. They must never be committed,
# and must never be visible to chezmoi as source state.
nvim-pack-lock.json
lazy-lock.json

# macOS
.DS_Store



# Omarchy migrations drop LazyVim-shaped files into ~/.config/nvim, which is a
# chezmoi symlink to nvim/ in this repo — so they land HERE. Example:
# /usr/share/omarchy/migrations/1781587663.sh does
#   install -m 0644 .../remote_clipboard.lua "$HOME/.config/nvim/lua/config/..."
# guarded only by [[ -d $nvim_config_dir ]], which is TRUE through the symlink.
#
# This config has no lua/config/ at all (its files are lua/options.lua etc), and
# `install` is used without -D, so that copy currently FAILS rather than
# succeeding into the repo. Do not create nvim/lua/config/ — not even a
# .gitkeep. Its absence is the real guard; this rule is the backstop, and only
# covers NEW files. For writes through the symlink into files that are already
# tracked, see the post-update hook in .chezmoiscripts/assets/.
nvim/lua/config/
